WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.603
-Every day, Donald Trump
continues to prove

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.471
that he's an increasingly
erratic President

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.672
who's unfit for his job.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.642
And now he's apparently
working even fewer hours

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.977
and neglecting urgent issues.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.346
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:18.251
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.286
Since the publication
of "Fire and Fury,"

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.088
the explosive book about his
first year in the White House,

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:25.825
President Trump has been
battling the growing impression

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.360
that even his closest aides

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.696
believe him to be dangerously
unfit for office.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.430
And they obviously
have a very strong case

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.465
since Trump knows virtually
nothing about the job.

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:36.502
But you would think that a man
who ran on a platform

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.939
of pure patriotism and who spent
months lecturing athletes

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.940
about respecting
the national anthem

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.044
would, at the very least,
know the words to the anthem.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.078
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.247
And yet Trump seemed lost

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.115
as he tried to sing along
to the anthem

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:52.118
before last night's National
College Football Championship.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:56.656
-♪ Oh, say, can you see ♪

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.359
♪ By the dawn's early light ♪

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.494
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:06.732
♪ What so proudly we hailed ♪

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:11.203
♪ As the twilight's
last gleaming ♪

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:16.042
♪ Whose broad stripes
and bright stars ♪

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.744
♪ Through the perilous fight ♪

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.413
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.216
-Oh, my God.
Trump sings the national anthem

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.718
the way the rest of us
sing "Despacito."

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.153
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.255
♪ Despacito ♪

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.558
♪ Muh, na-na-na-na-na, muh-ito ♪

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.025
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.260
Seriously,
how can you be President

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.928
and not know the words
to the national anthem.

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:37.996
That's like Peyton Manning
not knowing the words

00:01:37.996 --> 00:01:40.199
to the Nationwide jingle.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.602
♪ Nationwide
is somethin' somethin' ♪

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.270
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.939
Now just two weeks
into the new year,

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.374
Trump faces a series
of urgent tasks

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.343
that deserve every ounce
of his attention,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.379
from keeping the government open
to protecting DACA recipients

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:56.049
to fully funding the Children's
Health Insurance Program

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.117
to providing electricity
to millions of Puerto Ricans

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.518
who are still without it.

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:02.521
And yet he's apparently
spending even less time working

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:03.790
than he did before.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.592
The website Axios obtained
Trump's private schedule,

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:09.896
not the public ones that
his staff puts out, and found...

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.046
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.282
I'm sorry.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.784
He starts his day at 11:00 a.m.?

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.152
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.922
Is he the president or
a lunch waiter at Olive Garden?

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.923
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.724
All I do is make fun of him,

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:41.361
and I still
have to be here at 9:00 a.m.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:42.828
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:45.298
Just take Trump's
private schedule from this week

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.333
as an example
of how little he works.

00:03:14.993 --> 00:03:17.029
Oh, my God. Trump might be
our first President

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:18.264
who works so little,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.766
he technically qualifies
for unemployment.

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:27.506
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:30.542
It's like Trump
isn't even the president.

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:32.912
He's more like Mike Pence's
out-of-work friend

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.880
who has to crash with him
for a while

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.382
till he gets back on his feet.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.751
He's the Dupree
of the white House.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:43.022
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.591
Deep cut.
That's a deep cut.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:48.360
Trump, of course, not only
defers all major policymaking

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.496
to his staff
and Republicans in Congress,

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:54.266
he's also so fragile and erratic
that he needs those same people

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:56.769
to go on TV
and lavish praise on him,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:04:00.139
as Senior Policy Adviser
Stephen Miller did on Sunday

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:03.709
in this now infamous interview
with CNN anchor Jake Tapper.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:07.179
-The reality is, the President
is a political genius

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:10.949
who won against a field of
17 incredibly talented people,

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:13.052
who took down the Bush dynasty,

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.221
who took down
the Clinton dynasty.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:18.691
All these so-called political
geniuses in Washington,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.560
whether it be
the big lobbying firms or --

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.262
-The only person
who has called himself a genius

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.530
in the last week
is the President.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.532
-Which happens
to be a true statement.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:30.202
A self-made billionaire
who revolutionized reality TV.

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:33.205
-And I'm sure he's watching and
he's happy that you said that.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:36.308
-I would be with the President
on a campaign plane

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:38.210
with a rally in 20 minutes,
and he would be able --

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.812
-You've already
made this point, Stephen.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.781
-He would be able
to come up with material

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.048
in the blink of an eye.

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:44.317
-You've already said that.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:47.353
-A self-made billionaire,
revolutionized reality TV,

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.021
and tapped
into something magical

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:51.256
that's happening
in the hearts of this country.

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:54.727
-Ugh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:58.597
I'd say Stephen Miller has
a boner, but he already is one.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:05.170
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.874
Seriously,
he looks like someone slapped

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.842
a couple of
googly eyes on a penis.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.977
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.746
Seriously, is there anyone
creepier than Stephen Miller?

00:05:14.746 --> 00:05:16.982
He wasn't born.
He just appeared after someone

00:05:16.982 --> 00:05:19.851
read an Edgar Allen Poe story
into a cracked mirror.

00:05:19.851 --> 00:05:20.886
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.555
Also, can we go back

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.757
to the first part of that clip
for a second?

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.259
-The President
is a political genius,

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:31.029
who won against a field of
17 incredibly talented people,

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:33.098
who took down the Bush dynasty,

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:35.067
who took down
the Clinton dynasty.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.201
-There's nothing worse

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:38.003
than someone
who pronounces it "din-iss-tee."

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.405
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.340
Miller claims --

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.542
Miller claims he's in touch
with the working class,

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.679
but he pronounces words
like a British dandy.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.113
What's next?
You gonna tell us

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:50.516
Trump checks his "mo-bile"
for this "shed-yule"

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.119
so he can have some "privicy"
during his "le-zure" time?

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.720
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.322
To borrow a phrase
Stephen Miller might use,

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.024
Stephen Miller is a wanker.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.792
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.828
With googly eyes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:04.897
Obviously, with googly eyes.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:08.300
Also, can I just say,
I'm tired of this talking point

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.735
Trump and his toadies
keep repeating,

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:12.805
that he beat a field of 17
incredibly talented people?

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.106
He did not.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:15.908
Let's not forget
the field he ran against

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.978
included a narcoleptic,
a malfunctioning robot,

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.546
a sentient butter sculpture,

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:25.117
and a guy who was almost
suffocated by his own hoodie.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.786
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:30.323
And when Trump sycophants
aren't available to go on TV

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.291
and stroke his ego,
Trump does it himself.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:35.627
Yesterday, he flew to Tennessee
to sign an executive order

00:06:35.627 --> 00:06:37.596
and speak
to the American Farm Bureau.

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:40.699
And at one point, he needlessly
lashed out at the media

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:43.435
and told the crowd
to look up his Twitter account.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:47.573
-I will sign two presidential
orders to provide broader

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:53.613
and faster
and better Internet coverage.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:57.783
Make sure you look up
@RealDonaldTrump, right?

00:06:57.783 --> 00:07:00.953
-I'm sorry, but it just
strikes me as unpresidential

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.523
to plug your
social-media accounts.

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:05.758
He sounds like the end
of a YouTube video.

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.392
"If you thought
this speech was dope,

00:07:07.392 --> 00:07:11.030
please like and subscribe
for more sick content."

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:15.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.771
One of the details Trump's aides
have repeated about him

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:21.573
to show that he's mentally unfit
for his job is his penchant

00:07:21.573 --> 00:07:24.042
for repeating the same handful
of stories over and over,

00:07:24.042 --> 00:07:26.445
and yet again yesterday,
he rambled on

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:29.281
about his 2016 election victory
and reminded the crowd

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:31.284
of his position on guns.

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:33.719
-We're restoring the rule of law

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:38.958
and protecting
our cherished 2nd Amendment.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.560
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.962
-Why are you
making the hand motion?

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:45.731
They know
what you're talking about.

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:48.067
The way Trump abuses
the 1st Amendment

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.703
makes me want to take advantage
of the 21st Amendment.

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:56.409
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:59.344
Trump is like a guy
playing charades

00:07:59.344 --> 00:08:01.881
who doesn't realize
he's not allowed to speak.

00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:04.950
"Movie, two words --
Star, Wars.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.719
Boom! We did it!
That was so fast!

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.720
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:11.490
But it isn't just that Trump
is growing increasingly erratic.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.025
He's also becoming more lawless.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:15.694
After repeatedly hectoring
his Justice Department

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:18.330
to investigate Hillary Clinton,
it seems the DOJ

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.965
is now doing exactly that.

00:08:19.965 --> 00:08:22.467
And on top of that, yesterday,
the Trump administration

00:08:22.467 --> 00:08:25.171
announced that it was cruelly
ending the humanitarian program

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.706
that allowed 200,000 people
from El Salvador to live here

00:08:27.706 --> 00:08:28.974
for more than a decade.

00:08:28.974 --> 00:08:30.242
He's working fewer hours

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:32.578
and neglecting the basic
responsibilities of his job,

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.880
and yet he's still
desperate for praise.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.482
In his speech yesterday,
he railed on about the election

00:08:37.482 --> 00:08:38.784
and his
administration's attempts

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.419
to roll back regulations

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:44.056
and insisted to the audience
that they were happy he won.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:46.959
-We're streamlining regulations
that have blocked

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:50.229
cutting-edge biotechnology,

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:55.634
setting free our farmers to
innovate, thrive, and to grow.

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:59.038
Oh, are you happy
you voted for me.

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:02.408
You are so lucky
that I gave you that privilege.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:03.642
-Ugh.
[ Audience groans ]

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:06.445
He's so --
He's so gross.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.315
I never thought I'd say this,
but bring back Stephen Miller.

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:10.516
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.184
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:15.688
[ Cheers and applause ]

